Package: spatialFolds
Title: Fast Data-Splitting for Spatial Cross-Validation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("First", "Last", , "blasbenito@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fast C++ toolset for spatial cross-validation and thinning of point data. Generates training and testing folds (Roberts et al. 2017 <doi:10.1111/ecog.02881>) using three methods: contiguous (rectangle-growing from distributed centers), blocks (grid-cell selection), and random (traditional splitting). Introduces a novel contiguous method that preserves spatial structure by growing rectangular folds from well-distributed center points. Provides spatial thinning to reduce point density while maintaining spatial coverage. Integrates with 'tidymodels' via 'rsample'-compatible resampling objects for use with model tuning workflows. Supports parallel execution via 'future' and progress tracking via 'progressr'.
